    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Local winds are caused by localized differences in temperature and pressure, affecting microclimates over small areas.",
        "Chinook is a warm, dry wind blowing down the eastern slopes of the Rocky Mountains, popularly termed the 'Snow Eater'.",
        "Harmattan is a dry, dust-laden wind blowing from the Sahara towards the West African coast, known as the 'Doctor' for providing relief from humid air.",
        "Sirocco originates in the Sahara Desert and crosses the Mediterranean Sea to Southern Europe, carrying red dust that causes 'Blood Rain'.",
        "Mistral and Bora are severe, cold, dry katabatic winds blowing from inland mountains toward the Mediterranean basin."
      ],
      "id": "o58rsx6"
    },
